  "content": {
    "id": "p41-25j-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A bag contains 2029 blue and 2029 red balls. Two balls are drawn at random and removed from the bag. If the colours match, a blue ball is added; if different, a red ball is added. This process repeats until one ball remains. Find the probability it is red.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$.\n\nThe number of red balls remains odd throughout.",
      "worked": "Let $R$ be the number of red balls. There are three possible cases at each step:\n\n• Two blue balls: $R$ is unchanged.\n\n• Two red balls: $R$ decreases by $2$.\n\n• One red and one blue ball: removing the red ball and adding a red ball leaves $R$ unchanged.\n\nThus the parity of $R$ is unchanged. Initially $R=2029$ is odd, so it remains odd. When only one ball remains, $R$ must therefore be $1$, so the final ball is red.\n\n$$\\Pr(\\text{final ball is red})=1.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
